    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d873">

                <pb facs="0696" n="614" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg614"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.112 B61/62.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Mexican Chargé
                        d’Affaires.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1911-07-15"><hi rendition="#italic">July 15,
                        1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 81.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to the embassy’s note of the 25th
                    of May stating that the authorities of El Paso have instituted proceedings
                    against the captors of Edwin Blatt and Lawrence Converse and against Ascension
                    Archuleta, the brother of one of the captors, and requesting that this
                    Government cause the release of these persons, I have the honor to inclose
                    herewith copies of a letter of the 1st instant and inclosure from the governor
                    of Texas,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d873-f1"/> from which you will observe that none
                    of the persons mentioned in your note is in prison in that State and that
                    Ascension Archuleta, who has been under arrest, has now been released as the
                    result of habeas corpus proceedings.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.],</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
